    <tags>bff-api,frontend,compose,data-integrity</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Created 2026-07-23 from dev UAT rounds 1+2. Root-cause evidence in the conversation + notes/uat-feedback-2026-07-23.md. BUG A is a no-errors violation (must-fix); BUG B confirmed NOT data loss (no fix). Deferred items documented in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r5/README.md (G6-G10).</origin>
    <justification>
      Existing: ComposeWorkspace.tsx triggerSave already has both a create-on-save `{contentModel}` path (born-in-editor
      first save) and a replace `{operationLog, baselineVersionId}` path. Extension: extend the replace path to send
      `{contentModel}` for born-in-editor docs (mirror the create path), and extend the replace ENDPOINT validation to
      accept `contentModel` — no new component. Cost-of-doing-nothing: a born-in-editor doc's 2nd in-session save throws
      a hard 400/404 error (violates the R4 no-errors bar) and each save mints a duplicate `sprk_document` record.
    </justification>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Fix the two UAT-surfaced issues and apply four UX polish items. Do NOT implement any deferred R5 feature
    (versioning dropdown, transient-mount projection unification, external-change banner, etc. — those are R5, see
    projects/spaarkeai-compose-r5/README.md G6-G10).

    === BUG A (CRITICAL — the no-errors fix) ===
    A born-in-editor (blank-page) doc: 1st save works (create-on-save → ComposeDocumentRenderer). The 2nd in-session
    save FAILS ("Provide the retained-original 'content' bytes, or … 'baselineVersionId' …") because it takes the
    op-log/replace path with NO valid baseline: `state.docxBytes` is null (born blank) and create-on-save returned the
    drive-ITEM id as VersionId (not a real SPE version). Fix so born-in-editor docs re-author via `{contentModel}` on
    EVERY in-session save (never entering the baseline-less op-log path):
    - SERVER: `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs` — the replace-path ("Save") validation (~line
      1139-1142) currently requires `content` OR `baselineVersionId`. Add acceptance of a non-empty `contentModel`
      (e.g. `hasContentModel = body.ContentModel is { Blocks.Count: > 0 }`) to the OR so a contentModel save is a valid
      dirty save. `ContentModel` is already mapped into the replace request (~line 1165) and `ComposeService`
      `ResolveSaveBaselineAsync` already returns `SynthesizeDocument(...)` when `ContentModel` is non-null
      (`ComposeService.cs:891-894`), skipping the reanchor/patch-engine blocks (both gated on `ContentModel is null`).
      Confirm the replace branch then does `ReplaceFileContentAsUserAsync` on the EXISTING item (same speDriveItemId) —
      i.e. it UPDATES, not creates.
    - CLIENT: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx` `triggerSave` replace
      branch (~line 1098-1120) — when the doc is born-in-editor (use the SAME discriminant as the create path's
      `bornInEditorRender`, i.e. `!state.docxBytes`), send `{ contentModel: editorRef.current.buildContentModel() }`
      (mirror the create-path spread ~line 1094-1096) INSTEAD of `operationLog`/`baselineVersionId`. Leave the loaded/
      imported (docxBytes present) path exactly as-is (it still sends op-log + baseline → tracked changes; do NOT
      regress REQ-2).
    - RESULT must hold: (a) a born-in-editor doc's 2nd..Nth in-session saves succeed with NO error; (b) they UPDATE the
      same `sprk_document`/SPE item (NO new duplicate record per save — the V1 born-blank fix); (c) born-in-editor edits
      remain clean/untracked in-session (correct — no original to diff), and redlines still work after reopen-from-Document.
    - ALSO verify the Assistant-upload flow: it mounts transient WITH `docxBytes` (uploaded bytes). Confirm whether its
      repeated saves also mint duplicate records (UAT round 1 showed 8). If the same `!state.docxBytes` discriminant does
      NOT cover it (because docxBytes is present), DO NOT force it here — instead confirm + DOCUMENT that the Assistant-
      upload duplicate path is the transient-identity issue resolved structurally by R5 G6 (note it in
      notes/uat-feedback-2026-07-23.md). Only born-in-editor (born-blank) duplicate prevention is in 039 scope.

    === BUG B (NO code change — confirm + document) ===
    "Redlines lost when Track Changes toggled off" is VISUAL ONLY (the toggle is a display-only decoration; imported/AI
    redlines are real marks, nothing stripped on save). Do NOT change persistence. (Optional clarity is R5.) Just
    re-confirm by reading `ComposeEditor.tsx` toggle + `TrackChangesExtension.ts` and state it in the report.

    === UX polish (P1-P4) ===
    P1: Make the Track Changes control an ICON-ONLY toggle (no text label) in `ComposeFormatToolbar.tsx`. Keep the
        aria-label for accessibility; keep the pressed/active state.
    P2: Rename the "Search for Document" CTA to "Open Document" (`ComposeEmptyState.tsx:291` + the handler/comment
        references in `ComposeWorkspace.tsx`). Label/text only — do not change behavior.
    P3: Make the Word menu a VERTICAL dropdown with labels "Open web" and "Open desktop" (the `onOpenInWord` /
        `onOpenInWordDesktop` items).
    P4: Confirm there is NO live "Push to Word" control that would hit the retired (036) endpoint. If a dead
        push-to-Word menu item/button exists, remove it. If the only Word items are the Open-in-Web/Desktop handoff,
        state that (nothing to remove).
  </prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack dev — Compose React client (TipTap save orchestration, Fluent v9 toolbar) + the BFF ComposeEndpoints/ComposeService save path. Understands the born-in-editor (renderer) vs loaded (op-log/engine) save split and REQ-1/REQ-2. Follows ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Born-in-editor docs save without error on every in-session save (no-errors bar restored) and update the same record (no duplicates for born-blank); loaded/imported docs still track (REQ-2 intact); P1-P4 polish applied; BUG B confirmed not-data-loss; Assistant-upload duplicate path documented as R5 G6. Build + tests + redeploy green.</goal>

